@* The filter panel both search pages are built on: a pinned, collapsible box of filters with Search and
   Reset below it and a result count beside them.

   The two pages were the same page twice - the same lede, the same panel, and a footer that matched
   character for character down to the limit warning. Only the filters, the repository and the result
   rendering ever differed.

   The re-entrancy guard deliberately stays on the page rather than moving in here. Both pages document
   why: `disabled` does not suppress a keystroke, and key repeat fires keyup once per repeat, so holding
   Enter overlapped two searches on one DbContext. IsRunning comes in and OnSearch goes out, so the check
   stays at the page's single entry point. *@

<CollapsiblePanel @ref="_panel" Heading="Filters" Pinned="true">
    <Summary>@Summary</Summary>
    <ChildContent>
        @Filters
    </ChildContent>
    <Footer>
        <div class="actions">
            <button class="primary" @onclick="OnSearch" disabled="@IsRunning">Search</button>
            <button @onclick="OnReset" disabled="@IsRunning">Reset</button>
            @if (HasSearched)
            {
                <span class="muted">@ResultCount result(s)@(ResultCount >= Limit ? " - narrow the filters, this is the limit" : "")</span>
            }
        </div>
    </Footer>
</CollapsiblePanel>

@code {
    private CollapsiblePanel _panel = null!;

    /// <summary>
    /// The filter controls.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public RenderFragment Filters { get; set; } = null!;

    /// <summary>
    /// What is being filtered on, named while the panel is shut.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Summary { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether a search has run, which is what decides between "no results" and "not searched yet".
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool HasSearched { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Disables both buttons while a search is in flight.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool IsRunning { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public int ResultCount { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The cap the repository applies, so the count can say when it has been reached.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int Limit { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnSearch { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnReset { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Shuts the filters, so the results a search has just produced start at the top of the viewport.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Called by the page rather than wired to the Search button here, because Enter in a filter box runs
    /// the same search without going through the button - the page's run method is the one entry point
    /// both paths share.
    /// </remarks>
    public void Collapse()
    {
        _panel.Collapse();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Reopens the filters, for a page that has just cleared them.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Reset leaves nothing to read on a shut panel - no results, and a summary that says "no filters set"
    /// - so the panel stays folded over an empty page until the operator opens it again. Reopening is what
    /// makes Reset look like it did something.
    /// </remarks>
    public void Expand()
    {
        _panel.Expand();
    }
}
